<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Maseca reduced.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Maseca reduced.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Lehman Brothers analyst Will Landers has reduced his rating for Mexico's Grupo Industrial Maseca to neutral from outperform.</p>
<p>-- &quot;While the fourth quarter results were in line with our expectations from a bottom line standpoint, sales volume and operating income was lower than we had expected,&quot; Landers wrote in a March 5 report.</p>
<p>-- Due to constraints arising from a quota system linked to a government subsidy for tortillas, &quot;we are not expecting more than a five percent increase in sales volume during 1997, with an EBITDA growth of around six percent for the year.&quot;</p>
<p>-- He set a 12-month price target of $18 per American Depositary Receipt.</p>
<p>-- Maseca's ADR opened down 1/8 to 15-7/8.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
